import Mathlib.RingTheory.Extension.Cotangent.Basic
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Regular.RegularSequence

/-!
# Left injectivity in Jacobi–Zariski for a regular-sequence presentation

Source: Stacks Project, More on Algebra, Tag 07D4, the “in particular” clause,
using Tags 062F and 07CX, and Algebra, Tags 00S1 and 00S2
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-jacobi-zariski-regular-sequence-left-injective).
-/

universe u v w

namespace Algebra

/-- Source: Stacks Project, Tag 07D4, with a regular-sequence presentation (Tag 062F).
(blueprint: lem-weil-pbc-jacobi-zariski-regular-sequence-left-injective)
The canonical conormal map carries the kernel of the base-changed differential into
`H1Cotangent A C`; its restriction is injective. Tensor factors are reversed by symmetry.

Proof:
1. Put `P = A[B]`, with kernel `I`, and `T = P[y₁,…,yₘ]`. The coefficient map
`q : T → B[y₁,…,yₘ]` is surjective with kernel `I T` by
lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-coefficient-map-kernel. The composite with `β` has kernel `K`,
and `K/(I T)` is generated by the given regular sequence. Inclusion `P → T` is a
morphism of presentations (lem-weil-pbc-nl-presentation-h1-functoriality).
2. By lem-weil-pbc-conormal-intersection-regular-quotient, `(I T) ∩ K² = (I T) K`.
Polynomial extension and right exactness of tensor identify `C ⊗[B] (I/I²)` with
`(I T)/((I T) K)`. Thus its map to `K/K²` is injective.
3. Send `x_b` to `[φ(b)]` and `y_j` to `[β(y_j)]` in `A[C]`. Choose lifts in `T`
of all elements of `C` for a map in the other direction. By
lem-weil-pbc-nl-presentation-h1-functoriality, the two composites induce identity
maps on H₁, so comparison with the canonical presentation is an H₁ isomorphism.
The cotangent spaces are identified with free modules by
lem-weil-pbc-polynomial-ring-kahler-basis-any-variables.
4. The degree-zero map for `P → T` includes the `dx_b` summands and commutes with
the differentials. Step 2 therefore restricts to an injection on the kernel of the
base-changed differential. Compose with step 3. Its conormal formula is
`c ⊗ (g mod I²) ↦ c • (φ♯(g) mod I²)`, exactly the required map, also the leftmost
map of lem-weil-pbc-jacobi-zariski-homology-sequence. -/
theorem jacobiZariski_left_injective_of_regularSequence
    (A : Type u) (B : Type v) (C : Type w)
    [CommRing A] [CommRing B] [CommRing C]
    [Algebra A B] [Algebra B C] [Algebra A C] [IsScalarTower A B C]
    (m : ℕ) (fs : List (MvPolynomial (Fin m) B))
    (hreg : RingTheory.Sequence.IsRegular (MvPolynomial (Fin m) B) fs)
    (β : MvPolynomial (Fin m) B →ₐ[B] C)
    (hβ : Function.Surjective β) (hker : RingHom.ker β.toRingHom = Ideal.ofList fs) :
    let P := (Generators.self A B).toExtension
    let Q := (Generators.self A C).toExtension
    let F := (Generators.defaultHom (Generators.self A B) (Generators.self A C)).toExtensionHom
    let d := P.cotangentComplex.baseChange C
    let g := (Extension.Cotangent.map F).liftBaseChange C
    ∃ u : LinearMap.ker d →ₗ[C] H1Cotangent A C,
      (∀ x : LinearMap.ker d, Q.h1Cotangentι (u x) = g x.1) ∧ Function.Injective u := by
  sorry

end Algebra
